  "schema:datePublished": "2026-03-13",
  "schema:description": "Uploaded files contain negative and positive ion mass spectra of hydrated clusters of naphthalene, 1-cyanonaphthalene, phenanthrene and anthracene; and optimized geometries of mixed naphthalene-water clusters (1-2 Np, 0-9 W for neutrals and 1 Np, 7-9 W for anions) appearing in the article and its supplementary information. The ab-initio calculations complement the experimental data and help further interpretation of the mass spectra.\n\nIn the experiment, cluster beam was formed in supersonic expansion. Beam was then ionized by electron ionization or electron attachment and mass spectra of ionized beam were recorded using reflectron time-of-flight mass spectrometer. For calculations, different structures of Np1,2 (H2O)0-9 were optimized at the wB97XD/aug-cc-pvdz level of theory in the Gaussian 16 package. Initial guesses were based on already published structures of other hydrated PAH structures.\n\nFolder Exp_MS contains data for the mass spectra in three file types: ascii with extension .asc - mass spectrum with mass calibration constants and spectrum resolution as a header; binary with extension .tfb - raw spectrum in time domain; text with extension .tfa - parameters of the detector. The files are contained in subfolders according to the date of experiment. An Excell spreadsheet with assignment of the spectra to article/SI figures is included. Folder Geoms contains coordinates in xyz format. The file names correspond to the structures shown in the Supplementary Information of the article.",
  "schema:keywords": [
    "Atomic, molecular and chemical physics (physics of atoms and molecules including collision, interaction with radiation, magnetic resonances, Mössbauer effect)",
